# ── Rust build artifacts (rebuildable; ~130G across target dirs) ──────────────
/target
/target-cuda
**/target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta

# ── Built GPU prover binaries (~1G; rebuild from the hemilabs forks + patches/) ─
/dist

# ── Benchmark data / outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
/benches

# ── Session scratch: soak logs + throwaway test binaries ─────────────────────
/scratchpad
*.log

# ── Large handoff archives (extracted copies live in hemiprove-*/ dirs) ──────
*.zip

# ── Nested git repos — independently versioned; they ride along with the ─────
#    directory/VM transfer, NOT this parent repo's history:
#      contracts/           Foundry Solidity project (own .git + submodules)
/contracts
#      vendor/risc0-sppark/  NO LONGER VENDORED. Cargo.toml now patches sppark to a
#                            pinned git rev of hemilabs/risc0-sppark, so cargo fetches
#                            it and a clean clone builds with no extra steps. A local
#                            checkout here is ignored so it can be used for testing
#                            (point the patch at a path temporarily) without being
#                            committed and silently diverging from upstream.
/vendor

# ── Editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
.DS_Store

# ── Foundry build outputs in the vendored contract reference (regenerable) ───
hemiprove-source/out/
hemiprove-source/out-deploy/
hemiprove-source/broadcast/
hemiprove-source/cache/
